# Four-ply info spelling from Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), read 2026-11-24:
# UCIEngine::on_update_full in src/uci.cpp and SearchManager::output_pv in src/search.cpp.
# fisher-r6y D41 and fisher-8hc.6 stage this spelling. D3-D6 supply the
# existing principal variation and allowances, with time at least one under D41.
# The fisher-2aj.2 sources below supply the retained scores, node counts and response order.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and fisher-l7f owner decisions from 2026-11-22.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Mate -1 nodes 782: in 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b, black must play h8g8,
# then h6g7 is checkmate. Python-chess counts 1, 21, 30 and 730 nodes at
# plies 1 to 4.
# Mate -1 nodes 1299: in 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b, black must play h8h7,
# then g5g7 is checkmate. Python-chess counts 1, 25, 45 and 1228 nodes at
# plies 1 to 4.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go depth infinite
# Rule 9 sends info before the reply to isready. The move waits for stop.
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for mate -1 nodes 782.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 782 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
< readyok
> stop
< bestmove h8g8
> unknown go infinite
# Rule 9 sends info before the reply to isready. The move waits for stop.
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for mate -1 nodes 782.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 782 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
# UCI go infinite and isready. No bestmove precedes readyok.
< readyok
> go
# The owner rejects a second go while there is a held move.
< info string {message:waiting for stop}
# The ignored command consumes its stop argument.
> setoption name Path value stop
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The owner rejects a replacement position while there is a held move.
< info string {message:waiting for stop}
> unknown stop
# UCI stop/bestmove releases the held move.
< bestmove h8g8
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for mate -1 nodes 782.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 782 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The owner keeps the original position, whose only legal move is h8g8.
< bestmove h8g8
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for mate -1 nodes 782.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 782 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The reference also kept the original position.
< bestmove {legal}
# The prefixed stop allows the engine and reference to follow the next position.
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for mate -1 nodes 1299.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 1299 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# Black's only legal move in the replacement position is h8h7.
< bestmove h8h7
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for mate -1 nodes 1299.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 1299 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> stop
> isready
# UCI ignores an idle stop and replies to isready.
< readyok
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
